  "title": "Week 37: A Journey Back in Time at the Estonian Open Air Museum",
  "date": "2025-09-04T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 37: A Journey Back in Time at the Estonian Open Air Museum\n\nToday I ventured to the Estonian Open Air Museum, a fascinating place just 8km from Tallinn's Old Town that's easily accessible by bus. 🚌\n\nThis museum is like a small village, and I spent nearly four hours exploring! It's an incredible look at Estonian rural life and nature, showcasing what farm life was like from 200 years ago right up to the modern era.\n\nA Glimpse into the Past 🐄\n\nCozy bird's nests\n\nA cozy bird's nest\n\nA bountiful vegetable garden\n\nA bountiful vegetable garden\n\nA scene of farm life\n\nA traditional 19th-century farmhouse\n\nA traditional 19th-century farmhouse\n\nA farm from the 19th century\n\nA majestic windmill\n\nA majestic windmill\n\nKeeping the wolves at bay\n\nKeeping the wolves at bay\n\nfish house by the sea\n\nA charming fish house by the sea\n\nsea view\n\nA peaceful sea view\n\nThe Animals of the Museum 🐰\n\nAfter seeing some of the cute animals on the farm, they also showed how they were prepared for meals! 😄\n\nA traditional lamp\n\nThe rabbits here are surprisingly big—about the size of two of my heads! 🤯\n\nGiant rabbits\n\nSoviet-Era History & Community Life 🏫\n\nA collective farmer building from the Soviet era\n\nA collective farmer building from the Soviet era\n\nAn old bus\n\nfireman's tower\n\nThe old fireman's tower\n\nThe schoolhouse\n\nThe schoolhouse",
